From: juniorverli <25966843+juniorverli@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 18:42:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] platform/surface: aggregator_registry: Drop absent HID
 nodes on Surface Pro 11

On the tested Surface Pro 11, Windows creates KIP HID instances 1, 3
and 5 (keyboard, touchpad and firmware update), but no instance 2 and
no Target_SAM/Category_HID device. Linux registers both the KIP pen-stash
endpoint and the SAM HID sensor endpoint unconditionally. Both fail to
load their nine-byte HID descriptor with -EPROTO (zero bytes assembled).

Remove those endpoints from the Denali group for this project's tested
cover. The pen-stash endpoint reports pen storage state; the pen digitizer
is a separate MSHW0484 device. This local removal is not evidence that
all interchangeable covers lack pen-stash support. Revisit the KIP node
when another cover is tested.

The SAM sensor removal also matches Dale Whinham's upstream fix:
https://lkml.iu.edu/2609.2/08839.html

Keep descriptor validation in surface_hid unchanged.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5
Assisted-by: Codex gpt-6.1-sol
---
 drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c b/drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c
index d37a7e4c6..a098cd5a6 100644
--- a/drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c
+++ b/drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c
@@ -412,10 +412,8 @@ static const struct software_node *ssam_node_group_sp11[] = {
 	&ssam_node_bat_main,
 	&ssam_node_tmp_sensors,
 	&ssam_node_hid_kip_keyboard,
-	&ssam_node_hid_kip_penstash,
 	&ssam_node_hid_kip_touchpad,
 	&ssam_node_hid_kip_fwupd,
-	&ssam_node_hid_sam_sensors,
 	&ssam_node_kip_tablet_switch,
 	NULL,
 };
